  "limitations": [
    "One fixed episode and six plan calls repeatedly replayed; no closed-loop success or task-quality conclusion.",
    "Ninety timings per configuration are repeated calls of the same six-request sequence, not independent tasks. p10/p90 are empirical sample quantiles, not confidence intervals.",
    "GPU operation duration sum is the mean over six calls in one separate profiled replay per configuration; it cannot be subtracted from the unprofiled wall-time median to estimate CPU time.",
    "All quantized tiers keep selected VLM Linear modules in W8A8, while the reference is full BF16; action deviations therefore include the VLM quantization effect and are not isolated DiT errors.",
    "W4 coverage counts 192 candidate Linear sites, not parameters, FLOPs or GPU kernels. Attention core remains floating; T10 is not a fully INT4 model.",
    "Unprofiled host-call timing includes CUDA-event instrumentation, stream synchronization, Backend bookkeeping and request-log I/O. It excludes separately timed VLM updates, RPC, simulator and scheduling.",
    "Git revision/dirty state and selected native binary for the external integer backend are unknown; the expected revision and observed module/library hashes are retained separately.",
    "The trace-based explanations are consistent with the code path but no independent ablation isolates each suspected cause; profiler submission timings do not causally account for all unprofiled wall-time differences.",
    "T9 has the lowest pooled median, but round variation and overlapping sample ranges do not establish a stable best configuration.",
    "The existing GPU suite has three dit_graph parameter failures; only its BF16 case was rerun and reproduced on the pristine base.",
    "Dependencies, checkpoint assets and dataset are not bundled. A portable clean-environment rerun has not been performed. Device clocks/power/temperature time series were not recorded."
